course: dictionary
lesson: 2164
title: Corny: silly, old-fashioned or too sweet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Corny is an everyday word for jokes, songs and films that are old-fashioned, silly or a bit too sweet. Sometimes it is a mild, friendly teasing word. Look at the clues around it. «A dad joke is a simple, corny pun.» A simple pun that makes everyone groan fits the idea of silly and old-fashioned.
explain: Swap in your meaning to check it. Try "A dad joke is a simple, silly, old-fashioned pun." It still makes sense, so your meaning is right. Corny can also describe feelings: «a corny love song» is too sentimental and soppy for some listeners.
explain: Some people say something is "corny but sweet". That means it is silly or too much, but it is kind-hearted too, so the feeling behind it is still nice.
fact: Corny means old-fashioned, silly or too sweet.
fact: «A corny joke» is one that makes people groan, like "What do you call a deer with no eyes? No idea!"
fact: «A corny love song» is too sentimental, sweet or soppy.
fact: Corny is informal, so you hear it in everyday talk and reviews rather than formal writing.
fact: In a rare sense, corny means of or full of corn, like a cornfield.
exercise: «A dad joke is a simple, corny pun.» What does corny mean here? | Very frightening | Very fast | *Old-fashioned and silly, the kind that makes people groan | Made of metal
exercise: Ruby says a film is corny. What might she mean? | Very long and boring | Dark and scary | *Too sweet and soppy | Loud, with lots of explosions
exercise: Which word means about the same as soppy, as in «a corny love song»? | Loud | Quick | *Sentimental | Cruel
test: Mia says «corny but sweet» means the joke is silly in a kind way. Is she right? | No, corny always means rude and unkind | *Yes, corny can mean silly, and the kindness makes it sweet | No, corny only means made of corn | No, it means very fast
test: Which phrase is the best swap for corny in «a corny joke»? | Hidden and secret | Brilliant and clever | *Silly and old-fashioned | Frozen solid
exam: What does the author mean by «part of the fun is that it's so bad» about dad jokes? | Dad jokes are boring and nobody likes them | Dad jokes are hard to understand | Dad jokes are only told at Christmas | *Dad jokes are meant to be silly and groan-worthy, and that is part of the fun
